<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa plans to pay 0.50 dmk dividend.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa plans to pay 0.50 dmk dividend.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German airline Deutsche Lufthansa AG said on Tuesday that it planned to pay an unchanged dividend on 1996 earnings and that it swung to a profit in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>In a mandatory bourse statement, released ahead of Wednesday's annual news conference, the group said its management and supervisory boards had suggested paying a 50 pfenning per share dividend on 1996 earnings.</p>
<p>The group's shares are nominally valued at five marks per share.</p>
</text>
